{"id":34514,"slug":"all-of-us-strangers","title":"All of Us Strangers","year":2023,"country":"United Kingdom","duration":105,"spine":1234,"url":"https://www.criterion.com/films/34514-all-of-us-strangers","cover":"https://s3.amazonaws.com/criterion-production/films/5e0ad41060ee1b9b9f3054854ddcce9b/VvTw4ZeLwWYLaTe2IoQuK1leAtBKFS_large.jpg","description":"A metaphysical exploration of queer love and loneliness, familial grief and healing, this delicate but audacious chamber drama confirms director Andrew Haigh’s gift for bringing complicated emotions to the screen. Isolated in a seemingly empty new high-rise, London screenwriter Adam (Andrew Scott) finds his solitary existence upended when he begins a passionate romance with the impulsive Harry (Paul Mescal), then reconnects with his parents (Jamie Bell and Claire Foy) in a reunion that pushes beyond the limits of time and space. Putting a deeply personal imprint on a novel by Japanese writer Taichi Yamada, Haigh reaches cosmic heights while never losing sight of the story’s achingly human heart.","boxset":0,"scraped":1,"directors":[{"name":"Andrew Haigh","slug":"andrew-haigh"}],"cast":[{"actor":"Andrew Scott","role":"Adam","slug":"andrew-scott"},{"actor":"Paul Mescal","role":"Harry","slug":"paul-mescal"},{"actor":"Carter John Grout","role":"Young Adam","slug":"carter-john-grout"},{"actor":"Jamie Bell","role":"Dad","slug":"jamie-bell"},{"actor":"Claire Foy","role":"Mum","slug":"claire-foy"},{"actor":"Ami Tredrea","role":"Waitress","slug":"ami-tredrea"}],"credits":[{"role":"Director","person":"Andrew Haigh","slug":"andrew-haigh"},{"role":"Written by","person":"Andrew Haigh","slug":"andrew-haigh"},{"role":"Based on the novel Strangers by","person":"Taichi Yamada","slug":null},{"role":"Produced by","person":"Graham Broadbent","slug":null},{"role":"Produced by","person":"Pete Czernin","slug":null},{"role":"Produced by","person":"Sarah Harvey","slug":null},{"role":"Executive producer","person":"Diarmuid McKeown","slug":null